content.text:
Now add extra lamps after existing loops. Find:
```
for (const z of ROADS_Z) {
  addLamp(-800, z + 60); addLamp(800, z - 60);
}
```
Add mid-block lamps before the light pool comment. Lamps at z = -470, -40, 390 for vertical roads, alternating x side. But careful not to light the whole city into many sprites: 4 roads × 3 z × 1 = 12; horizontal similarly 12 = 24. Fine.

Coordinates: for each vertical road center x, for z of [-460, 20, 470]? But horizontal roads at -595,-205,185,575; midpoints between: -400, -10, 380, 770. Use z = -400, -10, 380 (3). Place at x±54 alternating by index. Ensure not inside intersection.

For horizontal, x = -430, 20, 490? Vertical roads at -615,-235,145,525; midpoints -425, -45, 335, 715. Use -425, -45, 335.

Implement:
```js
[-400,-10,380].forEach((z,i)=> ROADS_X.forEach((x,j)=> addLamp(x + ((i+j)%2?54:-54), z)));
[-425,-45,335].forEach((x,i)=> ROADS_Z.forEach((z,j)=> addLamp(x, z + ((i+j)%2?54:-54))));
```
That's 12 + 12 = 24 lamps. Total lamps 16 (intersections ×4=16? Actually for each x,z 2 lamps = 32) + 8 edges + 24 = 64.

Point pool 7.

Traffic glows: add in makeCar. Insert after taillights loop:
```js
for (const sx of [-1,1]) {
  const hg = new THREE.Sprite(new THREE.SpriteMaterial({map:glowTex,color:0xffe4b0,transparent:true,opacity:.5,blending:THREE.AdditiveBlending,depthWrite:false}));
  hg.position.set(sx*.6,.8,2.3); hg.scale.set(4,4,1); g.add(hg);
  const tg = new THREE.Sprite(...red, opacity .45, scale 2.6);
  tg.position.set(sx*.62,.8,-2.25); g.add(tg);
}
```
Sprites count 4 × 17 = 68. Fine.

Window emissive 1.05 → 0.8.

Also neon sign height lower. Find `sign.position.set(face ? x + w / 2 + 0.3 : x, 4.8 + rnd() * Math.min(18, h * 0.5), ...)`. Change to 5 + rnd()*8. Sign width maybe Math.min(w*0.6, 12). Good.

Apply.

