```
Rain noise buffer 3s; lowpass 1200; gain .018. Engine: two oscillators? Use one sawtooth + lowpass + gain; frequency update. Add tire skid? no.

In updatePlayer driving: if(audio) { freq = 48 + abs(speed)*2.2; audio.engine.frequency.setTargetAtTime(freq, now, .06); gain .015 + throttle*.03? use .02; } else gain .0.
Engine should only sound when in car; on foot mute.

Call startAudio in play click.

Need to guard browser latency; setTargetAtTime exists. Use audio.ctx.currentTime.

Implementation:
```js
let audio=null;
function startAudio(){
 if(audio) return;
 try{
  const AC=window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext; if(!AC) return;
  const ctx=new AC();
  // rain
  const buf=ctx.createBuffer(1, ctx.sampleRate*3, ctx.sampleRate);
  const d=buf.getChannelData(0); for(...) d[i]=(Math.random()*2-1)*0.5;
  const src=ctx.createBufferSource(); src.buffer=buf; src.loop=true;
  const lp=ctx.createBiquadFilter(); lp.type='lowpass'; lp.frequency.value=1400;
  const rg=ctx.createGain(); rg.gain.value=0.03;
  src.connect(lp).connect(rg).connect(ctx.destination); src.start();
  // engine
  const osc=ctx.createOscillator(); osc.type='sawtooth'; osc.frequency.value=60;
  const ef=ctx.createBiquadFilter(); ef.type='lowpass'; ef.frequency.value=380;
  const eg=ctx.createGain(); eg.gain.value=0;
  osc.connect(ef).connect(eg).connect(ctx.destination); osc.start();
  audio={ctx,osc,eg,rg};
 }catch(e){}
}
```
Update in updatePlayer driving:
```js
if(audio){ const now=audio.ctx.currentTime; audio.osc.frequency.setTargetAtTime(46+Math.abs(car.speed)*2.4, now, .08); audio.eg.gain.setTargetAtTime(.018+Math.abs(car.speed)*.00025, now, .1);}
```
Else mute engine:
```js
if(audio) audio.eg.gain.setTargetAtTime(0, now, .15);
```
Rain gain maybe .02.

On endGame, fade audio? Engine off via on foot. Fine.

