Now test. Also I should verify mission completion and mobile. Let's do a combined test with page eval performing teleports and waits:

1. Reload + start.
2. Teleport stage 0 → wait 300ms; stage changes. Then stage1 → wait; stage2 → wait; stage3 → wait; overlay should show NIGHT COMPLETE after 900ms. But each teleport must happen after the previous mission processed. Use async eval with delays:
```js
(async()=>{ const B=BH; const wait=ms=>new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,ms));
 B.player.pos.set(-615,0,-655); await wait(300);
 B.player.pos.set(525,0,-655); await wait(300);
 B.player.pos.set(525,0,575); await wait(300);
 B.player.pos.set(-615,0,575); await wait(1600);
 return {stage:B.stage, cash:document.getElementById('cash').textContent, overlay:!document.getElementById('start').classList.contains('hidden'), title:document.querySelector('#start h1').textContent};
})()
```
Note: checkMission runs every frame; teleporting near markers triggers. But the stage 0 marker at (-615,-655) is exactly where the player car? Teleport on foot. After stage 0->1, player remains at marker 0; the next teleport to marker1 works. Stage 2 triggers wanted and police; stage 3 triggers completion.

Then screenshot completion overlay. That verifies the full loop.

But earlier the police/health might kill the player before final? We teleport quickly; cops spawn 180 away and won't reach. Stage 3 stage teleports and ends.

Also check if stage increments correctly (the checkMission uses player.pos distance < 9; teleports exactly).

Then mobile: `playwright-cli resize 390 844` then screenshot. But resizing changes desktop viewport; CSS media max-width 700 shows touch. Verify layout. Then maybe reload for final desktop.

Also check FPS: run eval counting rAF for 1s:
```js
()=>new Promise(res=>{let n=0;const t0=performance.now();function f(){n++; if(performance.now()-t0<1000) requestAnimationFrame(f); else res(n);} requestAnimationFrame(f);})
```
Return FPS. In SwiftShader likely low (~10-20). If very low, consider optimizations. Let's measure.

